## Local Setup

### 1. Clone the repo
```bash
git https://github.com/hubautomation2026/skoda-parts-Assignment5-2026.git
cd Assignment Automation
```

### 2. Install dependencies
```bash
npm install
```

### 3. Install Playwright browsers
```bash
npx playwright install --with-deps chromium
```

### 4. Create your `.env` file
```bash
cp .env.example .env
```
Then fill in your values:
```dotenv
BASE_URL=https://www.skoda-parts.com

VALID_EMAIL=test555@test.com
VALID_PASSWORD=abcdef12345

INVALID_EMAIL=wrong@example.com
INVALID_PASSWORD=wrongpassword123
```

---

## Running Tests

```bash
# Run all tests (headless)
npm test

# Run with browser visible
npm run test:headed

# Run specific suite
npm run test:login
npm run test:register
npm run test:search

# Debug mode (step through)
npm run test:debug
```

---

## Allure Report

```bash
# Run tests then open live Allure report
npm run report

# Or separately:
npm test
npm run allure:generate
npm run allure:open
```

