## CI/CD — GitHub Actions

### How it works

Every push to `main` or `develop` automatically:

1. Installs Node.js + dependencies
2. Installs Playwright + Chromium
3. Reads secrets → creates `.env`
4. Runs all Playwright tests
5. Generates Allure report


### Setting up GitHub Secrets

Go to: `GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret`

| Secret name      | Value                          |
|------------------|-------------------------------|
| `BASE_URL`       | `https://www.skoda-parts.com` |
| `VALID_EMAIL`    | test555@test.com         |
| `VALID_PASSWORD` | abcdef12345                 |
  `INVALID_EMAIL`  |     wrong@example.com
`INVALID_PASSWORD` |    wrongpassword123


